description:
## Goal

Land one complete function-head warning vertical slice: demanded semantic analysis publishes typed retractable evidence through the ordinary fact ledger, and an exact retained request returns its diagnostic snapshot through the existing ProductMemo lifecycle.

## Atomic model gate

Before production changes, specify and test the smallest final data model:

- a typed semantic warning identity for a function-head match site; neither code/message/span nor rendered type text participates in identity;
- a typed evidence value for reachable `Dispatch Fail`;
- the producing `AnalyzeActivation(ActivationKey)` attempt as the ordinary contributor through `AttemptOutcome`/`JobEffects`;
- OR support and exact last-support retraction through the existing World fact-claim ledger, with no root-owned or warning-owned support graph;
- source-version provenance as an exact dependency separate from semantic identity;
- one retained diagnostic-snapshot product per exact retained request/root in ProductMemo, whose membership follows existing request/product/fact dependency edges rather than enumerating World, roots, functions, activations, or sources.

The evidence and retained consumer must land together. Do not introduce a shadow fact, temporary emitter, scan, or queue between them.

## Semantic producer

`AnalyzeActivation` already evaluates every correlated `ActivationInputs` row with `calculate_dispatch_reachability`. In the same completed attempt that publishes `ActivationAnalysis`, contribute function-head warning evidence iff the accumulated typed answer can reach `Dispatch Fail`. Do not add a derivation that wakes after `ActivationAnalyzed`; warning production is part of the work already demanded.

Contracts participate only where ordinary reached-call contract application refines or rejects an actual `ActivationInputs` row. There is no contracted/uncontracted coverage fork and no independent contract-domain enumeration.

Multiple demanded activations may contribute the same semantic site. Product projection deduplicates by typed identity; withdrawal of one ordinary producer preserves the warning while another contribution remains.

## Retained delivery

The diagnostic snapshot is presentation data retained by ProductMemo, not a World warning cache. It reads the exact warning evidence and provenance reachable from that retained request. Equal reproduction keeps its allocation and generation; an unchanged request may emit the retained value but performs zero producer/product evaluation and no deep copy. A warning/provenance change invalidates only exact diagnostic dependents; warning-only movement must not invalidate equal executable/backend/native content.

## TDD

Prove first:

- quicksort `append/2` and `qsort/1` produce no evidence or rendered warning;
- a demanded non-list row that can hit `Dispatch Fail` produces exactly one warning;
- removing that caller retracts it; re-adding it restores the same semantic identity with current provenance;
- two activations/demands supporting one site retain it until the last ordinary contribution leaves;
- an unobserved `@spec` overload and a cold function produce no coverage work, fact, diagnostic, dependency, or product movement;
- a broad demanded runtime/public boundary remains conservative only because its actual row is `any`;
- guarded fallthrough follows typed reachability;
- identical request preserves warning and snapshot allocation/generation with zero evaluations, wakes, allocations, or copies;
- unrelated replacement moves nothing; location-only replacement moves provenance/snapshot only;
- FIFO, LIFO, and permuted publication produce semantically and byte-identical evidence/rendering.

Use causal telemetry already owned by attempts, facts, and products. Add a durable typed event only if an acceptance assertion is otherwise impossible; do not add a warning-specific counter as authority.

## Required cutover and deletion

- Remove `source_diagnostics::check_function_clauses` and the `DefineFunction` function-head warning path.
- Remove `contract_has_reachable_fail`, `FunctionContract::input_domain_rows` if it has no remaining semantic consumer, and the `EntryDispatch` wait added solely for whole-contract coverage.
- Remove tests/docs asserting unobserved contract members are checked.
- Do not add a warning side map, warning queue, root scan, diagnostic retry registry, second support graph, private diagnostic cone, or compatibility adapter.

Update pattern-matching, semantic-fixpoint, pipeline, diagnostic, fact, product, and user-facing documentation in the same commit. Full focused, causal, replacement, fixture, CLI, formatting, check, and strict-Clippy gates pass.
